#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
# knife-sidecar-helper: the ONLY way the Smart Knife app user starts, stops and inspects its docker sidecars on a
# hardened host. The app user is not in the docker group (docker access = root on the host).
#
# Threat model: the app (user `knife`) may be fully compromised. Through this helper it can then only run a fixed set of
# `docker compose` verbs on the fixed sidecar ids below, against compose bundles that ROOT installed under
# /etc/samurai-knife/sidecars/<id>/ after validating them (`sync`, run by the owner with sudo). Nothing the app sends is
# ever interpolated into argv, a path or a compose file: the request is parsed against allow-lists and mapped to argv
# built from constants. Root's copy of the bundle is the only one docker reads.
#
# Modes
#   serve                 socket-activated (systemd knife-sidecar.socket, Accept=yes): fd 0/1 = one client connection
#   sync <id> [--yes] [--dry-run]
#                         root CLI: validate the app's staged bundle ($STAGING_DIR/<id>/: compose.yaml, secrets.env,
#                         assets/) and install it under $BUNDLE_ROOT/<id>/ (root-owned)
#   check <id>            root CLI: sync --dry-run
#   uninstall <id> [--force]
#                         root CLI: remove an installed bundle (refuses while its containers exist, unless --force)
#   hash <id>             print the installed bundle hash (same value the app compares against)
#
# Wire protocol (serve): the client sends ONE line `<verb> [<id> [<flag>...]]\n` (ASCII, <= 200 bytes, tokens
# [a-z][a-z0-9-]*). The helper answers with lines `o <text>` (docker stdout), `e <text>` (docker stderr / helper
# messages) and finally `x <exit code>`. Closing the connection aborts the running docker command (process group killed).
# Exit codes: 64 bad request, 69 bundle not installed / runtime unavailable, 75 busy (another op holds the id's lock),
# 77 peer not allowed, 124 timeout; anything else is docker's own exit code.
#
# Configuration: /etc/samurai-knife/sidecar-helper.conf (KEY=VALUE, root-owned, not group/world-writable). When NOT
# running as root (tests), KNIFE_SIDECAR_HELPER_CONF may point at another file; root ignores the variable.
#
# Contract: docs/DEPLOY.md "Sidecars without the docker group". Tests: tests/sidecar_helper.test.mjs.

